Subject: [PATCH 0021] Prism: no abort closing a tab with the spaces-mode
 chrome collapsed

GetAvailableWidthForTabContainer() falls back to
parent()->GetAvailableSize(this).width().value() when no width callback is
installed. In the spaces window mode (patch 0020) the tab strip's chrome
is collapsed, the parent produces no available size (nullopt), and
std::optional::value() on it aborts the browser process under the
hardened libc++ (_LIBCPP_HARDENING_MODE_EXTENSIVE ->
__libcpp_verbose_abort). Reachable by closing a tab mid-mode: window
close, Cmd+W, or CDP Target.closeTarget (TabStrip::RemoveTabAt ->
StartRemoveTabAnimation -> GetAvailableWidthForTabContainer).

Fall back to the container's current width: the remove animation runs at
the frozen width, which is invisible while the mode is active anyway.

diff --git a/chrome/browser/ui/views/tabs/tab_container_impl.cc b/chrome/browser/ui/views/tabs/tab_container_impl.cc
index b3cef86166..8cd6b5f364 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/ui/views/tabs/tab_container_impl.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/ui/views/tabs/tab_container_impl.cc
@@ -694,9 +694,15 @@ void TabContainerImpl::CompleteAnimationAndLayout() {
 int TabContainerImpl::GetAvailableWidthForTabContainer() const {
   // Falls back to views::View::GetAvailableSize() when
   // `available_width_callback_` is not defined.
-  return available_width_callback_
-             ? available_width_callback_.Run()
-             : parent()->GetAvailableSize(this).width().value();
+  if (available_width_callback_) {
+    return available_width_callback_.Run();
+  }
+  // Prism (spaces window mode, patch 0021): with the chrome collapsed the
+  // parent cannot produce an available size, and .value() on the nullopt
+  // aborts under the hardened libc++ when a tab is closed mid-mode (window
+  // close, ⌘W, CDP Target.closeTarget). Run the remove animation at the
+  // frozen current width instead — the strip is invisible anyway.
+  return parent()->GetAvailableSize(this).width().value_or(width());
 }
 
 void TabContainerImpl::EnterTabClosingMode(std::optional<int> override_width,
